      "message": "Superficially, this is a special case of behavior ordinarily handled in `read_byte` and `write_byte`, but I\u0027m wondering if it can be more generic. If the fail register is `FAIL_ALL_REG`, then I would expect any transaction to fail immediately, without having to evaluate the register. Could we handle all cases of `FAIL_ALL_REG` here, independent of length, and only handle specific register failures in the byte functions?",
